#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183914 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "9815dede-5c47-5430-a58a-218313f78412" :question/math-academy-id "e-10014" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-2x^2 - 4x = 1.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $x^2 + 2x + 1$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\nx^2 + 2x + 1 = (x + 1)^2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-4x & =1 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+2x) & =1 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 1x) & =1 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 1x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2}) & =1 \\\\ -2[(x+1)^{2}-{1}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ -2[(x+1)^{2}-1] & =1 \\\\ -2(x+1)^{2}+(-2)(-1) & =1 \\\\ -2(x+1)^{2}+2 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $2$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x+1)^{2}+2 & =1 \\\\ -2(x+1)^{2}+2-2 & =1-2 \\\\ -2(x+1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =\\frac{(-1)}{(-2)} \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ |x+1| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184083 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Positive Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "6e12005d-4652-532c-a715-3ab9d9ad3618" :question/math-academy-id "e-7139" :question/problem "Write the equation $2x^2 - 6x = 1$ in the form $(x+p)^2 = q,$ and hence solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we divide out by the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-6x & =1 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-3x) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-3x & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot x & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4} & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-\\dfrac32$ and $q=\\dfrac{11}{4}.$ Now, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{4}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{2}| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{11}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184084 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Negative Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "9dfe0c3a-2c54-5270-ab0d-0d2dad09a199" :question/math-academy-id "e-7140" :question/problem "Write the equation $-2x^2+2x+1 = 0$ in the form $2(x+p)^2=q,$ and hence solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-2{x}^{2}+2x+1) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2x-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-2x-1 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2x & =1 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-x) & =1 \\\\ 2[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ 2[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}] & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}] & =1 \\\\ 2{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ 2{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\dfrac12$ and $q=\\dfrac32.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{1}{2}| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Negative Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51235c4b-9ea8-5be6-9202-8faae512d7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2,\\,z=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399769} {:answer/id #uuid "18c50e74-54e2-5b08-8781-bdac4e3eb829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2,\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $z=-\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399770} {:answer/id #uuid "0ef860dc-5a1c-5a5d-8cba-4a4b862a9b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=9,\\,z=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399771} {:answer/id #uuid "c6502671-64f9-549c-ad24-6af57af49c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=9,\\,z=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{9}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399772} {:answer/id #uuid "605403ec-6766-5b0b-898a-15f1f1697f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2,\\,z=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "605403ec-6766-5b0b-898a-15f1f1697f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2,\\,z=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399773} :answer-field/id #uuid "132377e4-a98b-5f45-bb48-4f5451b52524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0945056-0521-55d9-80fa-5db83ff53407" :question/math-academy-id "q-112612" :question/problem "The equation $-4{z}^{2}-16z-7=0$ can be written in the form $4(z+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{z}^{2}-16z-7) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{z}^{2}+16z+7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{z}^{2}+16z+7 & =0 \\\\ 4{z}^{2}+16z & =-7 \\\\ 4({z}^{2}+4z) & =-7 \\\\ 4[{z}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot z+{(2)}^{2}-{(2)}^{2}] & =-7 \\\\ 4[{(z+2)}^{2}-4] & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(z+2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =-7 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2}-16 & =-7 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2} & =-7+16 \\\\ 4{(z+2)}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=2.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(z+2)}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {(z+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(z+2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\ |z+2| & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ z & =-2\\pm \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-2-\\frac{3}{2}=-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ z & =-2+\\frac{3}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $z=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Positive Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023e85b9-b324-5fae-8b24-a993cf078c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=6,\\,$ $z=-1,\\,5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269286} {:answer/id #uuid "051cc304-af83-50b4-a01c-91d408eee4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=5,\\,$ $z=2,\\,3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269314} {:answer/id #uuid "9b05c443-66c4-5788-9945-5ae98a6cd27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=9,\\,$ $z=-1,\\,5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270638} {:answer/id #uuid "ec254ead-7c72-506d-8d45-a216984be5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=9,\\,$ $z=2,\\,3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271344} {:answer/id #uuid "f2794853-d747-5b28-8e9f-17e9eaced79d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=5,\\,$ $z=-1,\\,5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b05c443-66c4-5788-9945-5ae98a6cd27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$q=9,\\,$ $z=-1,\\,5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270638} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b14b80a-26a2-5d34-a91a-5c29354c2e02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "948cfe82-2b59-583b-87a6-8211c3b5ce23" :question/math-academy-id "q-141627" :question/problem "The equation $3{z}^{2}-15=12z$ can be written in the form $(z-p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, divide it by the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-15 & =12z \\\\ 3{z}^{2}-12z & =15 \\\\ 3({z}^{2}-4z) & =15 \\\\ {z}^{2}-4z & =5 \\\\ {z}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot z & =5 \\\\ {z}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot z+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {(z-2)}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(z-2)}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {(z-2)}^{2}-4 & =5 \\\\ {(z-2)}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=2$ and $q=9.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(z-2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |z-2| & =3 \\\\ z-2 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =2\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ba4407-03eb-51b1-b004-b940f852c317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269265} {:answer/id #uuid "03a57f9c-3706-5c7b-9183-93bf72cd124d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269301} {:answer/id #uuid "3a359fbb-bf86-5e11-909d-f780a241551a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269799} {:answer/id #uuid "ad957086-768b-5537-8625-1aa43a2bf2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270814} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0efdd1-5309-518f-b349-e728470eb25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a57f9c-3706-5c7b-9183-93bf72cd124d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269301} :answer-field/id #uuid "f092d464-9988-5471-9683-fb59377b140b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03b9f129-6f00-5dcf-9f10-c4784f08b856" :question/math-academy-id "q-141824" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-6{y}^{2}+24y=21.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${y}^{2}-4y+4$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-4y+4=(y-2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{y}^{2}+24y & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-4y) & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y) & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}) & =21 \\\\ -6[(y-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}] & =21 \\\\ -6[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+(-6)(-4) & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+24 & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $24$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-6),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(y-2)^{2}+24 & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+24-24 & =21-24 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-6)} \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ |y-2| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ y & =2\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290c2ed7-3b4a-5f80-9ab8-6d2264b502c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6\\pm \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269637} {:answer/id #uuid "5afc9e05-2f19-56d4-8fd8-4dd154cab168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270079} {:answer/id #uuid "911deb27-d995-5dea-8e24-824959937b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270530} {:answer/id #uuid "b53b11d7-ba13-5f62-b662-6e3b9d578056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3\\pm \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270880} {:answer/id #uuid "d400bdca-5156-56ca-8976-ce67bf79adee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d400bdca-5156-56ca-8976-ce67bf79adee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271133} :answer-field/id #uuid "44e5bd75-2087-50a4-836f-a79a60347260" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2ec4003-7bb2-5f7b-b2d0-ca23e28bb9c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141826" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-7{y}^{2}-42y=62.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${y}^{2}+6y+9$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+6y+9=(y+3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7{y}^{2}-42y & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+6y) & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y) & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) & =62 \\\\ -7[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =62 \\\\ -7[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+(-7)(-9) & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+63 & =62\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $63$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-7),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(y+3)^{2}+63 & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+63-63 & =62-63 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{(-1)}{(-7)} \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y+3)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{7}} \\\\ |y+3| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\ y+3 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\ y & =-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139d882d-3cd8-5591-95ab-4f02b364c9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269444} {:answer/id #uuid "27b5c406-c7ab-5ca1-8538-f5588287699a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269620} {:answer/id #uuid "412dd5fe-943d-5e9f-9270-682fb4738770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269859} {:answer/id #uuid "91c7e265-47ef-51f2-a502-687b1a4fa602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270539} {:answer/id #uuid "f39b5916-e78a-5378-beb3-0cc0c23fcae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "412dd5fe-943d-5e9f-9270-682fb4738770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269859} :answer-field/id #uuid "05523259-00ab-5145-bcab-f2aec15fcd8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1044f32f-7390-525d-94d0-30c2ecd3e1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-141829" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-4{x}^{2}+4x=-2.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{4}$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{4}={(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{2}+4x & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-x) & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x) & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =-2 \\\\ -4[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}] & =-2 \\\\ -4[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}] & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+(-4)(-\\frac{1}{4}) & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1 & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $1$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-4),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1 & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1-1 & =-2-1 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =-3 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-4)} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{1}{2}| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Negative Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fa7313a-7406-5abc-80c9-a30b143bd862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fa7313a-7406-5abc-80c9-a30b143bd862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288583} :answer-field/id #uuid "755bfc03-bd02-52ab-8aab-d56ea4d74101" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b6fcfc-869c-5714-9359-faf7c265b47a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65b6fcfc-869c-5714-9359-faf7c265b47a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288748} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf4fcaa-8406-516c-8a6c-82c8165c0bcf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33ef5193-2ee7-5e06-8117-a25f40f24818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33ef5193-2ee7-5e06-8117-a25f40f24818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288375} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c37bd49-077a-53a1-a295-f2ea33481465" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbf52275-b8bd-52b3-9c51-96b483c07a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf52275-b8bd-52b3-9c51-96b483c07a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289272} :answer-field/id #uuid "e031303d-1afc-5f05-b049-a9f58c47689f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "94af16d4-6673-5335-b83a-58895c41f826" :question/math-academy-id "q-218774" :question/problem "$$\n-4{x}^{2}+16x-11=0\n$$\n\nBy completing the square, the above equation is equivalent to$\\,\\,4(x\\,\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}, and the solutions are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-3}}\n$\\pm $\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{x}^{2}+16x-11) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-16x+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-16x+11 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-16x & =-11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-4x) & =-11 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{(2)}^{2}-{(2)}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ 4[{(x-2)}^{2}-4] & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2}-16 & =-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & =16-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {(x-2)}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}} \\\\ |x-2| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\ |x-2| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184191 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With a Positive Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9167cc56-875d-5acc-ad8d-cad3d2163a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q - p = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183488} {:answer/id #uuid "a68a8f2d-5168-5cf1-ab81-c997b6e4d80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q - p = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183489} {:answer/id #uuid "081faa93-c132-5520-a376-834527fdc8fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q - p = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183490} {:answer/id #uuid "203ffeff-1dab-5d06-9da7-77144536a71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q - p = 6"